{"availability":"available","full":"GoogleMapReact/google-map-react","name":"google-map-react","description":"Google map library for react that allows rendering components as markers :tada:","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":6476,"forks":848,"created":"2015-06-10T10:58:20Z","updated":"2026-02-17T16:42:57Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"http://googlemapreact.github.io/google-map-react/","topics":["component","google","map","maps","react"],"demo":"http://googlemapreact.github.io/google-map-react/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:04:52.216Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T21:04:52.216Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T21:04:52.216Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:04:52.216Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"curated-list","name":"Awesome React Components","url":"https://github.com/brillout/awesome-react-components"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T21:04:52.216Z","stars":6476,"forks":848}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["google-map-react is a component written over a small set of the Google Maps API. It allows you to render any React component on the Google Map. It is fully isomorphic and can render on a server. Additionally, it can render map components in the browser even if the Google Maps API is not loaded. It uses an internal, tweakable hover algorithm - every object on the map can be hovered.","It allows you to create interfaces like this example (You can scroll the table, zoom/move the map, hover/click on markers, and click on table rows)"],"features":["Instead of the default Google Maps markers, balloons and other map components, you can render your cool animated react components on the map.","It renders on the server. (Welcome search engines) (you can disable javascript in browser dev tools, and reload any example page to see how it works)","It renders components on the map before (and even without) the Google Maps API loaded.","There is no need to place a <script src= tag at top of page. The Google Maps API loads upon the first usage of the GoogleMapReact component.","You can access to Google Maps map and maps objects by using onGoogleApiLoaded, in this case you will need to set yesIWantToUseGoogleMapApiInternals to true"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GoogleMapReact/google-map-react/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"0782c8738824c50f28f438b9291376eae993e0b5b32efde708ba01a8e6cf3061","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T21:04:52.216Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:04:52.216Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"google-map-react is a component written over a small set of the Google Maps API. It allows you to render any React component on the Google Map. It is fully isomorphic and can render on a server. Additionally, it can render map components in the browser even if the Google Maps API is not loaded. It uses an internal, tweakable hover algorithm - every object on the map can be hovered.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GoogleMapReact/google-map-react/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"0782c8738824c50f28f438b9291376eae993e0b5b32efde708ba01a8e6cf3061","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GoogleMapReact/google-map-react/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T21:04:52.216Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-02-17T16:42:57Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GoogleMapReact/google-map-react/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T21:10:05.729Z","hash":"0782c8738824c50f28f438b9291376eae993e0b5b32efde708ba01a8e6cf3061","originalBytes":8334,"storedBytes":8334,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["example","map","source","google","hover","maps","npm","api","components","examples","google-map-react","react","local","new","render","any","bash","component","container","need","create-react-app","dev","develop","every","here","jsbin","link","make","markers","module","set","simple","src","try","add","algorithm","allows","app","browser","